# Requirements Management Rules

## Purpose
Standardize how requirement sets are created and maintained.

## When To Apply
Apply when creating or updating requirement documents.

## Location & Layout
Follow `requirements-package-standard.mdc` for the package layout
(`docs/requirements/<name>/{README,prd,specification}.md` plus optional
files), the `Version: x.y.z` field, and the verification/review contracts. Do
not restate that layout here, and do not date-stamp the folder or fork
`ru`/`en`/`ai` copies — one set of documents, versioned in place, is the
standard.

## Mandatory Behavior
1. Ask for target location and requirement folder name before writing.
2. Confirm naming convention before creation.
3. Reuse the existing package folder for the topic; update documents in place
   and bump their `Version` field rather than creating a parallel copy.
4. Document assumptions and open questions explicitly.

## Output Contract
- Use Markdown (`.md`) only.
- Keep sections explicit: context, scope, requirements, constraints, open questions.
- Code snippets must be fenced code blocks.

## Workflow
1. Capture request.
2. Clarify folder/location under `docs/requirements/<name>/`.
3. Create or update the package per `requirements-package-standard.mdc`.
4. Document assumptions and open questions.
5. Ask whether to apply changes.
